# Suppressions for tools/lint-privacy.py. One `path:pattern-name` per line, or
# `path:*` to skip a file entirely. The tool reports how many findings were
# suppressed, so this file can never silently hide everything.
#
# Keep this list short and justified. Every line is a place the backstop is
# switched off, and the reason has to survive someone reading it in a year.

# The linter's own source contains the keyword and institution lists as literal
# strings, so a naive substring scan matches itself. Excluding the detector
# from its own scan is correct; excluding anything else here would need a much
# better reason.
tools/lint-privacy.py:*

# ETHICS.md enumerates the categories of identifier that must never appear, in
# order to forbid them. Naming a category is not disclosing an instance.
ETHICS.md:clinical-keyword
ETHICS.md:institution-name

# The copyright line names the author deliberately, and the author's name is
# their public identity on a public repository. Suppressed here rather than
# removed from the name list, so the token stays guarded in every other file:
# a surname that is intentional in a licence header is still a leak in an
# evidence brief.
LICENSE:personal-name
CITATION.cff:personal-name
